.TH RAESIR 8 "2026" "raesir 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
raesir \- lightweight init system and service manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raesir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B raesir
is a minimal init system designed to run as PID 1. It mounts essential
filesystems, launches services in dependency order, reaps zombie processes,
applies cgroup v2 resource limits and exposes a Unix socket control
interface.
.PP
Service definitions are read from
.I /etc/raesir/services
in TOML format. YAML definitions and systemd
.I .service
units are supported when the corresponding compatibility modules are enabled
at build time.
.SH SERVICE DEFINITION KEYS
.TP
.B name
Service name. Defaults to the file name without extension.
.TP
.B description
Human readable description.
.TP
.B exec
Command line to execute. Required.
.TP
.B working_dir
Working directory for the service process.
.TP
.B env
List of KEY=VALUE environment variables.
.TP
.B type
Either
.B simple
(default) or
.BR oneshot .
.TP
.B restart
Restart the service when it exits.
.TP
.B restart_delay_ms
Delay in milliseconds before a restart. Defaults to 100.
.TP
.B restart_max
Maximum number of automatic restarts. 0 means unlimited.
.TP
.B after, requires, wants
Dependency declarations controlling startup order. Services within the same
dependency level are started in parallel.
.TP
.B memory_max, cpu_weight
Cgroup v2 resource limits written to
.I memory.max
and
.IR cpu.weight .
.TP
.B tty
Terminal device for console services. The service receives its own session
and controlling terminal, enabling getty-style respawn together with
.BR restart .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Power off the system.
.TP
.B SIGINT
Reboot the system.
.TP
.B SIGCHLD
Reap terminated children and apply restart policy.
.SH LOGGING
Messages are written to
.IR /dev/kmsg ,
to
.I /var/log/raesir.log
with size-based rotation, and per-service output is captured in
.IR /var/log/raesir/<name>.log .
.SH CONTROL INTERFACE
A Unix domain socket at
.I /run/raesir.sock
accepts the commands
.BR status ,
.BR list ,
.BR start ,
.BR stop ,
.BR restart ,
.BR reload ,
.BR enable ,
.BR disable ,
.BR rescan ,
.B loglevel
and
.BR protocol .
The socket is owned by root with mode 0600 and peer credentials are
verified. The protocol is versioned; the current version is 1.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/raesir/services
Service definition directory.
.TP
.I /run/raesir.sock
Control socket.
.TP
.I /var/log/raesir.log
Daemon log file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR servctl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
meigoc (https://github.com/meigoc)
